FactorValue: urothelial cancer of the bladder
FactorValue: renal cell carcinoma
FactorValue: radical prostatectomy
FactorValue: intensity-modulated radiation therapy
FractionIdentifier: fractions 4–7
FractionationMethod: Urine fractionation by bottom-up Optiprep density gradient centrifugation
FractionationMethod: size exclusion chromatography (SEC)-based separation of EV from iodixanol
FractionationMethod: A combination of SEC and top-down ODG
FragmentationMethod: higher energy collisional dissociation (HCD)
GradientTime: a 50-min gradient from 8% to 35% of solvent B
Instrument: Q Exactive HF Hybrid Quadrupole-Orbitrap Mass Spectrometer (Thermo Fisher Scientific)
IonizationType: nano‐electrospray ionization
Label: Label-free quantification (LFQ)
MaterialType: biofluid
MaterialType: tissue
Modification: Carbamidomethyl (C)
Modification: oxidation (M)
Modification: acetylation of the protein N-terminus
NumberOfMissedCleavages: two
NumberOfTechnicalReplicates: Three
Organism: homo sapiens
OrganismPart: urine
OrganismPart: prostate cancer tissue specimens
ReductionReagent: dithiothreitol
SamplingTime: 3 months after local treatment by radical prostatectomy or intensity-modulated radiation therapy
Separation: nanoflow HPLC system (Easy-nLC1000, Thermo Fisher Scientific) coupled to a Q Exactive HF Hybrid Quadrupole-Orbitrap Mass Spectrometer (Thermo Fisher Scientific)
Sex: men
